mp-code-review: drop the setup-matt-pocock-skills tracker dependency

Replaces the broken "tell the user to run /setup-matt-pocock-skills"
line and step 2's "fetched via the workflow in the tracker doc" clause
-- that tracker-setup skill is out of scope for this repo's distribution,
so both pointed at a config file that never exists here. scripts/tracker.py
detects the repo's remote (GitHub vs GitLab, reading the raw remote URL
directly so an SSH-alias rewrite rule never hides the real host --
confirmed live in this very environment), extracts issue/MR references
from commit messages, and builds the gh/glab command to fetch each one.
Also renames the skill to mp-code-review (frontmatter name, not just the
directory) to resolve the real naming collision with Claude Code's
built-in code review and Superpowers receiving-code-review -- the same
anti-collision name dotfiles already uses for the unmodified upstream
skill.

